      "t": "h",
      "text": "Maple Ridge 55+ Condos: streets and boundaries"
    },
    {
      "gen": "uq",
      "items": [
        [
          {
            "t": "All of Maple Ridge's known 55-plus strata condos are in one pocket, Fraserview Village around 116 Avenue and 225 to 227 Streets in East Central."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "t": "The village amenity address is 22610 116 Avenue, listed for Fraserview Village in the Maple Ridge–Pitt Meadows Seniors Resource Directory with cost stated as market value and a contact to a realtor for purchase information."
          }
        ]
      ],
      "pos": "end",
      "t": "list"
    },
    {
      "gen": "uq",
      "level": 2,
      "pos": "end",
      "t": "h",
      "text": "Maple Ridge 55+ Condos: rules that affect buyers"
    },
    {
      "gen": "uq",
      "items": [
        [
          {
            "t": "A Fraserview Village age bylaw is lawful only because it is set at 55-plus, the sole age threshold the Strata Property Act now permits, in sections 123.1 and 123.2."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "t": "A building summary that still says rentals are not allowed at Rosewood Court is out of date for long-term rentals, because British Columbia voided strata rental-restriction bylaws on November 24, 2022; short-term rentals can still be restricted."
          }
        ]
      ],
      "pos": "end",
      "t": "list"
    },
    {
      "gen": "uq",
      "level": 2,
      "pos": "end",
      "t": "h",
      "text": "Maple Ridge 55+ Condos: local details a buyer would not know"
    },
    {
      "gen": "uq",
      "items": [
        [
          {
            "t": "Royal Crescent Gardens at 11698 226 Street is a registered assisted living residence, legal operator Optima Retirement Services Ltd., in the provincial Assisted Living Registry — care housing near Fraserview, not a condo to buy."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "t": "Greystone Manor at 11657 Ritchie Avenue is a Park Place Seniors Living retirement residence, listed with 74 private suites with full kitchens and in-suite laundry; it is rental housing."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "t": "Maple Ridge Towers at 11929 222 Street and Maple Towers at 11841 222 Street are subsidized seniors rentals with income-based cost, so they appear in seniors directories beside Fraserview but are not purchase stock."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "t": "School catchments do not affect most Fraserview buyers, but a grandchild living with a resident under the under-19 exemption would be in School District 42, with catchments set by exact address."
          }
        ]
      ],
      "pos": "end",
      "t": "list"
    },
    {
      "gen": "uq",
      "level": 2,
      "pos": "end",
      "t": "h",
      "text": "Maple Ridge 55+ Condos: costs and taxes"
    },
    {
      "gen": "uq",
      "items": [
        [
          {
            "t": "For multi-residential properties the City's 2026 schedule lists a flat water fee of $815.62, which is the utility line a condo strata's budget reflects rather than a bill the owner pays directly."
          }
        ]
      ],
      "pos": "end",
      "t": "list"
    },
    {
      "gen": "uq",
      "level": 2,
      "pos": "end",
      "t": "h",
      "text": "Maple Ridge 55+ Condos: getting around"
    },
    {
      "gen": "uq",
      "items": [
        [
          {
            "t": "Haney Place Exchange, reached from 116 Avenue via 226 Street, is the transfer point for the R3 Lougheed Hwy RapidBus and routes 701, 743 and 744 toward Meadowtown and Pitt Meadows."
          }
        ]
      ],
      "pos": "end",
      "t": "list"
    },
    {
      "gen": "uq",
      "level": 2,
      "pos": "end",
      "t": "h",
      "text": "Maple Ridge 55+ Condos: risks and due diligence"
    },
    {
      "gen": "uq",
      "items": [
        [
          {
            "t": "Fraserview Village sits above River Road in the Port Haney area, so a buyer should check the lot against Schedule A of Floodplain Management Bylaw No. 8121-2026, which sets flood construction levels and setbacks city-wide."
          }
        ],
        [
          {
            "t": "Buildings from 1991 to 1997 are at the age where the depreciation report and contingency reserve fund matter most, so read both in the Form B package rather than relying on the current strata fee alone."
          }
        ]
      ],
      "pos": "end",
      "t": "list"
    },
